{title: 14 Engrandecido sea Dios}
{key: G}
{capo: 1}
{time: 4/4}
{lyricist: Henry S. Turrall (1867-1953)}
{composer: William Shrubsole, 1779 (1759-1829)}

{sov}
1. [G]Engrande[C]ci[G]do sea [D7]Dios en [G]es[C]ta [G]oca[D7]sión.[G]
[C]Ale[G]gres, [D7]jun[G]tos a una [D7]voz
[G]dad gloria, [Em]gloria, [G]gloria [D7]al [G]Dios [C]e[G]ter[D7]nal.[G]
{eov}

{sov}
2. [G]Durante el [C]día [G]que pa[D7]só, la [G]ma[C]no [G]del Se[D7]ñor[G]
[C]de muchos [G]ma[D7]les [G]nos sal[D7]vó:
[G]dad gloria, [Em]gloria, [G]gloria [D7]al [G]Dios [C]e[G]ter[D7]nal.[G]
{eov}

{sov}
3. [G]Él hasta [C]a[G]quí nos ayu[D7]dó, y [G]siem[C]pre [G]provee[D7]rá.[G]
[C]Con gra[G]ti[D7]tud, [G]placer y a[D7]mor
[G]dad gloria, [Em]gloria, [G]gloria [D7]al [G]Dios [C]e[G]ter[D7]nal.[G]
{eov}

{sov}
4. [G]A o[C]tras [G]almas salva, [D7]¡oh Dios! [G]Des[C]piér[G]talas, Se[D7]ñor;[G]
[C]es[G]cucha [D7]nues[G]tra peti[D7]ción,
[G]y [Em]salva, [G]sal[D7]va, [G]salva, [C]sal[G]va al [D7]peca[G]dor.
{eov}
